Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `objects.object_id`: primary key to join with the other tables.  
• `objects.department`: filter = 'The Libraries'.  
• `objects.title`: apply a case‑insensitive LIKE '%book%' filter.  
• `objects.metadata_date`: needs re‑formatting with FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%F', …).  
• `vision_api_data.object_id`: join key.  
• `vision_api_data.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints.confidence`: “cropConfidence”; must be > 0.5.

Typical conditions  
• `o.department = 'The Libraries'`  
• `LOWER(o.title) LIKE '%book%'`  
• `hint.confidence > 0.5`

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery SQL queries (each returns at most 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few rows from the objects table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show objects that belong to “The Libraries”
SELECT object_id, title, department
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'The Libraries'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Libraries objects whose title contains the word “book” (case‑insensitive)
SELECT object_id, title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'The Libraries'
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE '%book%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Display metadata_date formatted as YYYY‑MM‑DD
SELECT object_id,
       FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%F', metadata_date) AS metadata_date_fmt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'The Libraries'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Inspect the raw cropHints data for a few images
SELECT object_id, cropHintsAnnotation
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data`
WHERE cropHintsAnnotation IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Extract crop confidence values (>0.5) from the nested cropHints array
SELECT v.object_id,
       hint.confidence AS crop_confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS hint
WHERE hint.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Join objects with vision_api_data and show crop confidence
SELECT o.object_id,
       o.title,
       hint.confidence AS crop_confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`         AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS hint
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Apply the department filter in the join result
SELECT o.object_id,
       o.title,
       hint.confidence AS crop_confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`         AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS hint
WHERE o.department = 'The Libraries'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Add title filter and confidence > 0.5
SELECT o.object_id,
       o.title,
       hint.confidence
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`         AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS hint
WHERE o.department = 'The Libraries'
  AND LOWER(o.title) LIKE '%book%'
  AND hint.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL ANSWER – object_id, title, and formatted metadata date
SELECT o.object_id,
       o.title,
       FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%F', o.metadata_date) AS metadata_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`         AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(v.cropHintsAnnotation.cropHints) AS hint
WHERE o.department = 'The Libraries'
  AND LOWER(o.title) LIKE '%book%'
  AND hint.confidence > 0.5
LIMIT 20;
```
